  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThere is little change to the forecast. The H5 ridge will\nfinally begin to breakdown, but not before continued sweltering\nand record or near record breaking temperatures are forecast \nboth today and tomorrow. Forecast highs in the mid-upper 90s \nwill run 15-20 degrees above climo norms, and combine with dews\nin the 60s to output peak daily HI's right around the century \nmark; the Advisory was maintained due to the prolonged duration \nheat of the week, thru the weekend, for a heightened risk of \nhealth related impacts with virtually no relief from the \ndangerous heat realized all week. \n\nThe metamorphosis from our recent heat blast to more\nclimatologically normal readings will occur thanks to a cold \nfront that approaches tomorrow and makes passage tomorrow night-\nMonday. A transition day Monday occurs as the airmass is \nreplaced, with mid 80s (north) to mid 90s (south), while temps \nsettling around norms for the remainder of the week may well see\nmuch of us with highs in the upper 70s/around 80F daily over \nits back half. The price to pay to get there will be some mid \nchance to likely category pops that accompany the air mass \nreplacement, including a marginal risk of severe. Dew points\nmake an analagous fall as well, thru the 60s to potentially some\nupper 50s/around 60F appearance over th latter half of the \nweek.",
